# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What must NOT be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Two reasons: speed (web/android alone is 30 MB of Gradle output that the
# server image never touches) and safety (server/.env holds the Supabase
# password and JWT_SECRET — those belong in the host's environment panel, never
# baked into an image layer).
#
# Note on syntax: a bare `node_modules` would only match the one at the root,
# so every path pattern here is written with `**/` where it must match at any
# depth. Anything the image genuinely needs is COPY-ed explicitly in the
# Dockerfile, which is why this list can stay aggressive.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Installed and built inside the image, never copied in.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

# Secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Baked into the APK at build time, not into the server image: it pins
# VITE_API_BASE to the teacher's LAN address, which would make the hosted SPA
# call 192.168.1.10 instead of its own origin.
web/.env.production

# Local SQLite database, its journals, and the nightly copies.
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
server/data
server/backups

# Android project + the built APK (30 MB of Gradle, irrelevant to the server).
web/android
web/resources
StudentApp.apk
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# History, CI and docs — none of it changes the running image, and including it
# would bust the build cache on every documentation edit.
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
README.md
db

# Windows-only helpers.
build-apk.ps1
start.bat

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/.tmp

# The host reads these from the repository, not from the build context, so
# excluding them keeps a deploy-config edit from busting the layer cache.
# (The Dockerfile itself is deliberately NOT listed: some builders resolve it
# through the context, and a missing Dockerfile is a hard failure.)
render.yaml
fly.toml
